{"id": "EUVD-2026-101557", "enisaUuid": "f21eb5e4-e1ab-31e5-9135-4eb284acf57c", "description": "In Eclipse Vert.x versions [5.0.0,5.0.12] or [5.1.0,5.1.9] or [5.2.0, 5.2.0], the Vert.x HTTP/1.x decoder uses a canonicalization for well known HTTP headers, the canonicalization process interprets well crafted headers as headers of this list, allowing for instance Content-Xength to be interpeted as Content-Length.\n\n\n\nThis can be exploited for request smuggling purpose.\n\n\n\nThe impacted component is io.vertx:vertx-core.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T18:43:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:23:47", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-vertx/vert.x/security/advisories/GHSA-ch7p-g5pm-3gqx", "https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/cve-assignment/-/work_items/352"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-102479"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05edf571-0a94-3120-830b-81a9b3a22113", "product": {"name": "Eclipse Vert.x", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "5.1.0 \u22645.1.9"}, {"id": "4d543394-1f1b-3102-b887-6f22025b3ab4", "product": {"name": "Eclipse Vert.x", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "5.0.0 \u22645.0.12"}, {"id": "7bf0145b-89a6-36d6-9200-666598c99920", "product": {"name": "Eclipse Vert.x", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "5.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9f004997-86b8-3202-96a4-c0344a14c73f", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}